# AnalystRequest gate (hard rule)

- Cross-scope and contract-impact changes go **only through the System Analyst**.
- Developers and QA escalate with a structured **AnalystRequest**; they do **not** renegotiate requirements peer-to-peer (FE↔BE, QA↔FE/BE chat agreements are not source of truth).
- Only the System Analyst edits `docs/features/<feature-id>/requirements.md`. Others propose; analyst writes and bumps `Version:`.
- Cite the requirements **version** on every review and build. Work against a stale version is invalid.
- Blocking findings pause the affected scope (and any dependents the analyst marks) until status is `incorporated`, or `answered` with explicit “no requirements change.”
- File requests under `docs/features/<feature-id>/findings/<short-slug>.md` using the AnalystRequest skill/template.
